  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most critical uncertainty is whether a multimodal (RNA + image) model outperforms single-modality baselines, and what a reasonable multimodal baseline accuracy looks like. config_007 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, weighted fusion) tests this core hypothesis with a clean, interpretable setup: it combines both modalities using the cheapest RNA encoder (PCA) and the lighter image backbone (ResNet50), avoiding the added cost of multiprofile aggregation or transformer layers. This gives me a solid accuracy anchor to later compare against (a) single-modality configs to confirm multimodal benefit, (b) ViT-L vs ResNet50, (c) scGPT/scVI vs PCA, and (d) different fusion/aggregation strategies. Expected relative cost: low-to-moderate — ResNet50 is roughly half the parameter count of ViT-L, PCA encoding is negligible, singleprofile avoids multiprofile data overhead, and no aggregation module adds training time. This keeps GPU hours low, preserving budget for follow-up experiments that probe the most promising directions."
}

